From 59fa2261f49355d15ae5c6c58e47f101f822f2e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:18:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bedrock): manage Character Creator characters

Read the five account recipes and native Dressing Room catalog so players can select a character, browse owned pieces, and edit saved recipes. Use the native appearance PUT flow with a profile hash check and a readback for slot, piece, color, size, cape, and emote changes. Keep the settings profile and unrelated recipe fields intact.

Create new characters with the complete starter recipe captured from Bedrock 1.26.51, or copy an existing recipe into an empty slot. Delete a character by saving its base-only recipe. Both operations follow captured native request shapes; deletion keeps another saved character active. The four-position emote wheel uses saved recipe entries and native empty placeholders.

Bedrock 1.26.51 cape captures on the DressingRoom_Capes Store page and the appearance PUT flow showed that an equipped cape uses the catalog pack UUID without a piece suffix and sits before the four emote entries. A direct authenticated account test confirmed that equipping a cape adds one mesh and texture to the assembled GLTF model; the account was restored afterward.

Sequential native Size captures confirmed four fixed height entry pairs. Changing height removes the previous pair and saves the selected pair before the emote wheel. A separate arm-width capture changed only the base arm field from wide to slim while leaving cs_arm as wide. The account was restored to its original recipe after these captures.

The account API returns recipes rather than a Bedrock skin packet. Fetch the active character model as GLTF, convert its meshes and textures to static Bedrock geometry and an atlas, and persist it for login. Refresh that model after active character edits. The service model has no animated face, body animation, piece handles, or tint groups, so this is a static rendering until a source for those fields is available.
